(7680712, 1256477, 18197, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by willem:</b></div><hr/><i> It does have some black and whites, but predominantly a full nice range of midtones.  To me this is not high contrast. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for your thoughts. Obviously, we disagree. High contrast does not demand monochrome, or b&amp;w, or high key, or low key. There can be high contrast elements, even in a photo with lots of mid-tones. The seeds and fluff contrast very well, and in fact, the fluff and mid-tones do too.  Not interested in a debate, not trying to change your mind. Just explaining my logic in entering this photo.</td>', 'Originally posted by willem: It does have some black and whites, but predominantly a full nice range of midtones.  To me this is not high contrast.   Thanks for your thoughts. Obviously, we disagree. High contrast does not demand monochrome, or b&w, or high key, or low key. There can be high contrast elements, even in a photo with lots of mid-tones. The seeds and fluff contrast very well, and in fact, the fluff and mid-tones do too.  Not interested in a debate, not trying to change your mind. Just explaining my logic in entering this photo.', '2020-12-02 00:35:22.000000', NULL, 0),
